{"name":"Mystical Mist","hex":"#e5e2e3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mystical","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to mystics or mysticism.","Having a spiritual or magical significance that transcends human understanding."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mystical"},{"term":"mist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water or other liquid finely suspended in air.","A layer of fine droplets or particles."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form mist.","To spray fine droplets on, particularly of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mysticism","blocks":[{"text":"Mysticism encompasses religious traditions of human transformation aided by various practices and religious experiences. Popularly, mysticism is used synonymously with mystical experience, a neologism which refers to an ecstatic unitive experience of becoming one with God, the Absolute, or all that exists."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Hildegard_von_Bingen_Liber_Divinorum_Operum.jpg/330px-Hildegard_von_Bingen_Liber_Divinorum_Operum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mysticism"},{"title":"Mist","blocks":[{"text":"Mist is a natural phenomenon caused by small droplets of water aerosols suspended in the cold air, usually by condensation. Physically, it is an example of a dispersion, most commonly seen where water vapor in warm, moist air meets sudden cooling, such as in exhaled air in the winter, or when hot sauna steam is suddenly released outside. Mist occurs naturally as part of weather, typically when humid air comes into contact with surfaces that are much cooler. It can also be created artificially with aerosol spray dispensers if the humidity and temperature conditions are right."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mist"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Peter_Paul_Rubens_166.jpg/500px-Peter_Paul_Rubens_166.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Peter_Paul_Rubens_166.jpg/500px-Peter_Paul_Rubens_166.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" The Appearance of the Holy Spirit before Saint Teresa of Ávila, Peter Paul Rubens","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APeter_Paul_Rubens_166.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Khagdaev1.JPG/500px-Khagdaev1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Khagdaev1.JPG/1280px-Khagdaev1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Khagdaev1.JPG/500px-Khagdaev1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Buryat shaman performing a ritual on Olkhon Island","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKhagdaev1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Josep_Benlliure_Gil43.jpg/500px-Josep_Benlliure_Gil43.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Josep_Benlliure_Gil43.jpg/500px-Josep_Benlliure_Gil43.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Life of Francis of Assisi by José Benlliure y Gil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJosep_Benlliure_Gil43.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Abulafia.p